# Control plane repos (orchestration + configuration)

Use this rule **before** adding YAML, Bicep, jsonc, or PowerShell in either repo. Answer four questions: which pipeline deploys this folder, which environment and Azure scope, what the other repo must add, and whether an existing pipeline already covers it.

ADO project: `gemeente-den-haag` / `Azure Control Plane`.
Live composition pipelines live under ADO folder `\production` and run YAML from **configuration**. Pattern templates and IaC live in **orchestration**.

## Repo split (do not invert)

| Repo | Role | Put here | Never put here |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `azure-control-plane-orchestration` | Reusable templates, Bicep, PowerShell | `common/azure-pipeline-templates`, `common/bicep-resource-modules`, `common/common-powershell-scripts`, `deployment-patterns/<pattern>/*.yml` + `.bicep` + scripts | Subscription IDs, tenant IDs, MG IDs, service connection names, env-specific jsonc |
| `azure-control-plane-configuration` | Env values + thin pipeline entry | `deployment-patterns/<pattern>/azure-pipelines.yml` (DNS: `azure.pipelines.yml`), `*.jsonc`, `common-configuration/*-env-vars-metadata.yml` | Forked copies of orchestration templates or Bicep modules |

`engineering.mdc` still describes split entries (`build-artifacts.yml`, `release-canary.yml`, `release-production.yml`). **On `main` today** each live pattern uses **one** `azure-pipelines.yml` that `extends` the orchestration pattern and loops `Canary` then `Production`. Prefer that shape unless the team has already moved that pattern to split YAML **on `main`**.

## Pipeline contract (every composition YAML)

Configuration entry always:

1. Declares `resources.repositories` named `azure-control-plane-orchestration` (`type: git`, `name: azure-control-plane-orchestration`).
2. `extends` `/deployment-patterns/<pattern>/<pattern>.yml@azure-control-plane-orchestration`.
3. Passes directories under `@self`: `bicepParametersDirectory`, `metadataDirectory`, `environmentConfigurationDirectory: /common-configuration`.
4. Passes jsonc **filenames** (build flattens folders) plus `environments: [Canary, Production]`.
5. Bootstraps service-connection variables so YAML expansion can see them; runtime values come from env metadata.

```yaml
# Debug SOP only (never merge a personal feature ref)
# ref: refs/heads/feature/<user>/<id>-<title>
# Merge-ready: refs/heads/main or a release tag (refs/tags/vX.Y.Z or refs/tags/latest)
```

**On configuration `main` today** (verify before bumping): `tenant-control-plane`, `tenant-iam-vending`, `platform-network-dns`, `platform-observability` pin `refs/tags/v1.10.0`. `platform-network-hub`, `platform-network-control-plane`, `platform-network-data-plane` pin `refs/tags/v1.16.0`. `landing-zone-firewall-rules` pins `refs/tags/latest`.

Triggers on those entries include `feature/*` and the pattern path. Deploy stages skip pull requests (`Build.Reason != PullRequest`). ADO environments are `canary` and `production` (lowercased job `environment:`).

## Shared stage shape

1. **Build** (`common/azure-pipeline-templates/bicep-build-stage.yml`): checkout configuration + orchestration, copy jsonc to `configuration-artifacts` (flatten unless landing-zone-vending), copy `common/` and `deployment-patterns/` IaC. Despite the name, this stage does **not** run `bicep build` on `main`.
2. **Canary Deployment** then **Production Deployment**: load `global-vars-metadata.yml` plus `${{ lower(environment) }}-env-vars-metadata.yml`. Jobs use `bicep-deployment-jobs.yml` (token replace `#{ACPP_*}#` then `bicepDeployment.ps1`) or `powershell-deployment-jobs.yml`.

`bicepDeployment.ps1` on `main` calls `New-AzTenantDeployment` / `New-AzManagementGroupDeployment` / subscription deploy directly. There is **no** separate what-if YAML stage. `engineering.mdc` still requires production `build → what-if → deploy`; do not invent a new pipeline to satisfy that. Extend the shared deploy templates if what-if is added.

ADO environment gates are the production approval boundary (segregation of duties).

## Environments and Azure scopes

Pipeline **environments**: Canary and Production. Values live in configuration `common-configuration/`:

- Shared names/abbreviations: `global-vars-metadata.yml` (`ACPP_INTERMEDIATE_ROOT_MANAGEMENT_GROUP` = GDH `mg10001`, location `westeurope`).
- Per env: `canary-env-vars-metadata.yml`, `production-env-vars-metadata.yml` (service connections `tnt-tcp-<can|prd>-sp001` identity, `sp002` tenant/infra; platform management/security/connectivity **subscription IDs belong only here**, never in orchestration).

Management groups (configuration `tenant-hierarchy.parameters.jsonc`, not orchestration):

| ID | Display | Role |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `mg10001` | GDH | Intermediate root. Compliance + remediation assignments. AVNM/DNS policies. |
| `mg10002` | Legacy | Temporary. **Compliance only** (same jsonc). Hardcoded today on the tenant-control-plane composition YAML as `legacyIntermediateRootGroupManagementGroupId`. |
| `mg20001` | Platform Landing Zone | Under GDH |
| `mg20002` | Application Landing Zones | Under GDH |
| `mg20003` | Sandbox | Under GDH |
| `mg20004` | Decommissioned | Under GDH |
| `mg30001`..`mg30004` | Connectivity, Identity, Management, Security | Under platform |
| `mg30005`..`mg30006`, `mg30008` | Online, Corp, Artificial Intelligence | Under app LZs |
| `mg30007` | Quarantine | Default MG for new subscriptions |

Platform subscription **tokens** (IDs only in env yaml): `ACPP_PLATFORM_CONNECTIVITY_SUBSCRIPTION_ID` (hub, AVNM, DNS, firewall rules), `ACPP_PLATFORM_MANAGEMENT_SUBSCRIPTION_ID` and `ACPP_PLATFORM_SECURITY_SUBSCRIPTION_ID` (observability).

